   = help: the trait `FitsIn<_>` is not implemented for `Option<i64>`
   = note: `encrypt` takes a value the encoding never refuses: a narrower integer, an `f32`, bytes, or a typed value such as a `NaiveDate`
   = note: a value the encoding can refuse (an integer that may be out of range, text, a `DateTime<Utc>`, or any other `Encrypt` value) goes through `encrypt_checked`, which checks it while the program runs
   = help: the following other types implement trait `FitsIn<T>`:
             `&Vec<u8>` implements `FitsIn<vitaminc_ore::target::Bytes>`
             `&[u8; N]` implements `FitsIn<vitaminc_ore::target::Bytes>`
             `&[u8]` implements `FitsIn<vitaminc_ore::target::Bytes>`
             `&chrono::naive::date::NaiveDate` implements `FitsIn<vitaminc_ore::target::Date>`
             `&f32` implements `FitsIn<vitaminc_ore::target::F64>`
             `&f64` implements `FitsIn<vitaminc_ore::target::F64>`
             `&i128` implements `FitsIn<vitaminc_ore::target::I128>`
             `&i16` implements `FitsIn<vitaminc_ore::target::I128>`
           and $N others
